1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:31,610 --> 00:01:33,990
Once again, I owe you.

37
00:01:33,990 --> 00:01:36,200
You're not going to pay me
back anyway, are you?

38
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:39,870
About the materials they wanted under
Freedom of Information,

39
00:01:39,490 --> 00:01:42,290
First Interim Report Concerning
Objects Referred to as Angels
and the Human Instrumentality Project

40
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:42,660
I handled it by giving them
some falsified data.

41
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:45,330
The government is quietly
pursuing legal action,

42
00:01:45,330 --> 00:01:47,420
but that will be blocked any day now.

43
00:01:47,420 --> 00:01:52,130
So, should I do something about
that project as well?

44
00:01:52,130 --> 00:01:55,550
No, judging by the material you sent me,
there should be no problem.

45
00:01:55,550 --> 00:01:57,630
Then, I'll continue as planned.

46
00:01:57,680 --> 00:02:00,390
EPISODE 07
THAT WHICH
IS MANMADE

47
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,270
Good morning.

48
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:16,570
G'morning.

49
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:28,870
This is the way to start your morning!

50
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:30,630
Not with coffee?

51
00:02:30,630 --> 00:02:37,550
A traditional Japanese breakfast begins
with rice, miso, and sake.

52
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:39,550
You mean YOUR traditional breakfast.

53
00:02:39,550 --> 00:02:41,220
What's that supposed to mean?

54
00:02:41,220 --> 00:02:45,390
Besides, who was supposed
to cook this morning anyway?

55
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:50,270
Now I know why you're still single
at your age, Miss Misato.

56
00:02:50,270 --> 00:02:52,810
Well, excuse me for being coarse.

57
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:54,610
And sloppy too.

58
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:57,110
Leave me alone!

59
00:02:57,110 --> 00:02:57,860
I'm done.

60
00:03:00,450 --> 00:03:02,660
Are you really going to come
to school today?

61
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:06,080
Of course. It's your parent-teacher
meeting after all.

62
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,950
But you're so busy with your work.

63
00:03:07,950 --> 00:03:11,250
Don't worry about it. This is
part of my job too.

64
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:12,710
It's part of your job?

65
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:18,050
Yes?

66
00:03:18,050 --> 00:03:22,550
Oh, thanks for coming all this way!
Yes, wait just a minute.

67
00:03:22,550 --> 00:03:25,560
Miss Misato, please don't go out like that.

68
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:27,100
It's embarrassing.

69
00:03:27,100 --> 00:03:28,020
Okay, okay.

70
00:03:31,390 --> 00:03:33,480
Good morning, Ikari!

71
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:35,940
We're taking off now, Miss Misato!

72
00:03:35,940 --> 00:03:37,190
See you!

73
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:40,610
Let's get going!

74
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:46,950
Ah, sarcasm.

75
00:03:46,950 --> 00:03:50,960
Well, I guess it's good that he's loosening up
and expressing himself more.

76
00:03:56,170 --> 00:03:57,130
Yes?

77
00:03:57,130 --> 00:04:00,130
He just left. I'll leave guarding him
from here to you.

78
00:04:12,690 --> 00:04:14,270
She's arrived!

79
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:22,110
Cool! Who is she?

80
00:04:22,110 --> 00:04:23,320
Ikari's guardian?

81
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:26,660
What?! He's got a babe like that
for a guardian?!

82
00:04:26,660 --> 00:04:27,330
They're such dorks.

83
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:33,210
Miss Misato really is awesome!

84
00:04:33,210 --> 00:04:34,370
You think so?

85
00:04:34,370 --> 00:04:37,920
It's even more amazin' that she's
Nerv's Ops Director.

86
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:39,380
You think so?

87
00:04:40,170 --> 00:04:44,680
It's just a counseling session but
my mother had to dress up!

88
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:43,760
Good thing that Shinji's
such a baby, Kensuke.

89
00:04:43,760 --> 00:04:46,640
Yeah, Shinji's no rival for us!

90
00:04:44,680 --> 00:04:46,640
Don't you think she's silly?

91
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:50,180
You guys don't know what a slob she is.

92
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:54,100
Man, I wish I had a girlfriend like her!

93
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:56,150
I bet you'd have a tough time.

94
00:04:56,150 --> 00:04:58,110
You just don't get it, do you, Mr. Big Shot?

95
00:04:58,110 --> 00:05:01,280
All right, we'll leave protecting
the Earth to you,

96
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,610
so you leave Miss Misato to us!

97
00:05:06,110 --> 00:05:08,620
Unit 01 has achieved the
required cooling level.

98
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:10,990
Please shift operations to Stage 2.

99
00:05:09,530 --> 00:05:11,870
Protecting the Earth...

100
00:05:11,870 --> 00:05:13,040
That's what Eva is for.

101
00:05:14,370 --> 00:05:16,540
Come to think of it, just what is the Eva?

102
00:05:16,540 --> 00:05:18,750
The entry plug smells like blood.

103
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:21,550
But I feel so relaxed here. Why?

104
00:05:22,550 --> 00:05:25,760
In the end, I don't know anything.

105
00:05:26,470 --> 00:05:29,220
What's the status of Unit 00's
bio-chest components?

106
00:05:29,220 --> 00:05:30,930
It was seriously damaged.

107
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:34,430
We'll make a new one, but it'll barely fit
within our supplementary budget.

108
00:05:34,430 --> 00:05:38,560
Will our job get any simpler once
we get Unit 02 from Germany?

109
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:40,230
It could go the other way.

110
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:43,190
Disposing of the Angel on the surface
isn't cheap, right?

111
00:05:43,190 --> 00:05:46,280
Yeah, this place is really tight
when it comes to money.

112
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:48,570
We're talking about the fate of mankind here!

113
00:05:48,570 --> 00:05:49,990
It can't be helped.

114
00:05:49,990 --> 00:05:52,240
"Man cannot live by Eva alone."

115
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:55,370
All those survivors need money to live too.

116
00:05:55,370 --> 00:05:56,830
Budgets...

117
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:58,580
So, is the Commander off
to another conference?

118
00:05:58,580 --> 00:06:01,130
Yes, he's on the plane now.

119
00:06:01,130 --> 00:06:04,050
It's nice and quiet here
when he's not around.

120
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:15,560
Excuse me. Since we're sharing the flight,
do you mind if I sit here?

121
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:19,940
The revised budget for the sample collection

122
00:06:19,940 --> 00:06:21,770
passed quite easily, didn't it?

123
00:06:21,770 --> 00:06:25,570
The Committee's main concern
is for their own survival.

124
00:06:25,570 --> 00:06:27,700
They aren't stingy when their
own lives are at stake.

125
00:06:27,700 --> 00:06:31,530
After all, the basis of their argument was
that no more Angels would appear.

126
00:06:31,530 --> 00:06:33,950
Oh, I have one more piece of good news.

127
00:06:33,950 --> 00:06:39,290
All members of the UN except the U.S.
have approved the budget for Eva Unit 06.

128
00:06:39,290 --> 00:06:42,630
Well, it's probably just a matter of time
for the U.S. as well.

129
00:06:42,630 --> 00:06:46,800
That country is allergic
to unemployment, after all.

130
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:48,130
And what about your country?

131
00:06:48,130 --> 00:06:50,430
We will participate beginning with
the construction of Unit 08.

132
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:53,720
The plans for the second installation
project are still viable.

133
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:57,980
However, there is the problem of
not yet having found a pilot.

134
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:00,810
The Angels have appeared once again.

135
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:03,940
We have no choice but to defeat them.

136
00:07:03,940 --> 00:07:08,440
We don't want another
Second Impact either.

137
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:13,370
Then you're saying that the Second Impact
that evaporated Antarctica wasn't...

138
00:07:13,370 --> 00:07:18,700
Yes, the history texts say it was
a disaster caused by a huge meteorite,

139
00:07:18,410 --> 00:07:23,380
Giant Explosion at the South Pole

140
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:21,870
but sometimes the truth
has been covered up.

141
00:07:21,870 --> 00:07:23,960
Fifteen years ago at the South Pole,

142
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:28,300
mankind discovered the humanoid being
known as the first "Angel".

143
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:29,720
However, in the middle of the investigation,

144
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:32,840
for reasons unknown,
there was a huge explosion.

145
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:35,600
That is the real truth behind
the Second Impact.

146
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:38,060
Then, what we're doing here...

147
00:07:38,060 --> 00:07:41,350
To prevent a probable Third Impact
from happening.

148
00:07:41,350 --> 00:07:44,560
That is the purpose of Nerv
and the Evangelions.

149
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:48,070
By the way, the event will occur
tomorrow as scheduled.

150
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:50,860
I understand.

151
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,540
Good morning.

152
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,380
Good morning.

153
00:08:07,380 --> 00:08:10,050
I'm going to Old Tokyo on business.

154
00:08:10,050 --> 00:08:13,220
I'll probably be back late tonight,
so have delivery for dinner.

155
00:08:13,220 --> 00:08:14,390
Later.

156
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:17,050
Okay.

157
00:08:22,810 --> 00:08:26,520
Abandoned Zone 28 (Center of Old Tokyo)

158
00:08:31,150 --> 00:08:35,610
It's hard to believe this used to be
the flourishing capital of Tokyo.

159
00:08:35,610 --> 00:08:37,120
We're here.

160
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:41,790
Of all places, they didn't have to hold it here.

161
00:08:41,790 --> 00:08:44,580
So, is the SSDF involved in this project?

162
00:08:44,580 --> 00:08:48,540
The Strategic Self Defense Force?
No, they're not allowed to interfere.

163
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:50,380
No wonder they're doing as they please.

164
00:08:57,800 --> 00:09:01,220
Celebrating JA Completion
Announcement Commemoration

165
00:08:58,550 --> 00:09:01,220
Thank you very much for taking the time
out of your busy schedules today

166
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:05,140
Nerv Party

167
00:09:01,220 --> 00:09:05,140
to attend the demonstration
of the new product

168
00:09:05,140 --> 00:09:07,980
that we at Japan Heavy Chemical Industries
are so proud of.

169
00:09:08,940 --> 00:09:14,400
Later, you will be observing the offical
demonstration from the control room,

170
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:17,200
but we'll be taking your questions here.

171
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:17,780
Yes!

172
00:09:17,780 --> 00:09:20,990
The famous Dr. Ritsuko Akagi.

173
00:09:20,990 --> 00:09:23,160
It is our honor to have you here.

174
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:25,410
May I ask a question?

175
00:09:25,410 --> 00:09:27,330
Of course, certainly!

176
00:09:27,330 --> 00:09:29,000
According to our earlier briefing,

177
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:31,050
this unit is equipped with an
internal nuclear reactor, correct?

178
00:09:31,050 --> 00:09:33,800
Yes, this is one of our product's
most distinguished features.

179
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:38,010
150 days of consecutive
operating power is assured.

180
00:09:38,010 --> 00:09:42,770
But from a safety perspective, isn't
incorporating a nuclear reactor

181
00:09:42,770 --> 00:09:46,350
into a weapon designed for
hand-to-hand combat risky?

182
00:09:46,350 --> 00:09:50,360
It's better than a weapon that
won't work for over five minutes.

183
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:53,530
But in an emergency there could be
problems with remote control.

184
00:09:53,530 --> 00:09:55,070
Still it's more humane than a system

185
00:09:55,070 --> 00:09:59,030
that induces great mental stress,
and causes mental instability.

186
00:09:59,030 --> 00:10:01,280
Cut it out. This just makes
you look childish.

187
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:03,240
And there's still the issue of manual control.

188
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:07,540
I believe that it is safer than a most
dangerous weapon

189
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,380
that can go out of control and run wild.

190
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:12,380
A weapon that cannot be controlled
is utter nonsense!

191
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:15,510
It's like a woman in hysterics!

192
00:10:15,510 --> 00:10:17,090
Unmanageable!

193
00:10:19,550 --> 00:10:22,100
That is what our pilots
and technology are for.

194
00:10:22,100 --> 00:10:26,600
You're not saying that science and the
human heart will tame that beast?

195
00:10:26,600 --> 00:10:27,850
Are you serious?

196
00:10:27,850 --> 00:10:29,650
Yes, of course I'm serious!

197
00:10:29,650 --> 00:10:32,520
Because Nerv depends on something
as unreliable as the human heart,

198
00:10:32,520 --> 00:10:35,400
you've allowed a loss of control
such as we just saw.

199
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:38,900
That's why the UN had to approve
that colossal supplementary budget.

200
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:42,450
As a result, over 20,000 people
in several countries are starving.

201
00:10:42,450 --> 00:10:44,990
On top of which, regardless of it having been
such a critical incident,

202
00:10:44,990 --> 00:10:47,540
the causes of it are still unknown?

203
00:10:47,540 --> 00:10:51,290
I wish you would at least fulfill that much
of your responsibilities!

204
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:58,170
I envy you. Nerv is protected by a super-legal
act that allows you to avoid responsibility.

205
00:10:58,170 --> 00:10:59,720
It doesn't matter what you say.

206
00:10:59,720 --> 00:11:03,220
The fact is that only Nerv's weapons have
the ability to defeat the enemy.

207
00:11:03,220 --> 00:11:05,220
You mean the AT field?

208
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,850
That's just a matter of time as well.

209
00:11:07,850 --> 00:11:10,440
Nerv's day in the sun will not last forever.

210
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:13,980
Nerv Party

211
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:20,360
Damn it! Idiots! Who do those
fat cats think they are?!

212
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:24,070
This is just payback for getting
cut out of the profit loop!

213
00:11:24,070 --> 00:11:26,790
I am so pissed!

214
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:28,330
Damn it! Damn it!

215
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:30,920
Stop that. This just makes you look childish.

216
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:34,000
He's just a show-off, begging for praise.

217
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,300
He's a small man.

218
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:39,420
But how did he even know
about the AT field?!

219
00:11:39,420 --> 00:11:41,300
There's been a huge leak
of classified material.

220
00:11:41,300 --> 00:11:43,220
What the hell is Intelligence doing?

221
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:59,740
We will now begin the JA activation test.

222
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:02,200
There is absolutely no danger.

223
00:12:02,990 --> 00:12:05,740
Make yourselves comfortable,
and watch through that window.

224
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:09,120
Ready to activate.

225
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:10,290
Start the test.

226
00:12:10,290 --> 00:12:11,620
Open all power circuits.

227
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:13,330
Pressure levels nominal.

228
00:12:13,330 --> 00:12:15,040
Coolant system circulation nominal.

229
00:12:15,040 --> 00:12:16,840
Release the control rods.

230
00:12:16,840 --> 00:12:18,840
The reactor has exceeded threshold levels.

231
00:12:18,840 --> 00:12:20,630
Output is nominal.

232
00:12:20,630 --> 00:12:21,880
Begin walk cycle!

233
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:24,390
Walking. Forward ahead, slow.
Forward right leg.

234
00:12:24,390 --> 00:12:26,930
Roger. Walk, forward ahead slow.

235
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,010
Forward

236
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,010
Stop

237
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,010
Reverse

238
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,010
Slow

239
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,010
Half
Speed

240
00:12:26,470 --> 00:12:28,010
Flank
Speed

241
00:12:26,930 --> 00:12:28,010
Forward right leg.

242
00:12:33,890 --> 00:12:35,060
Balance is nominal.

243
00:12:35,060 --> 00:12:36,480
Power core status nominal.

244
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:37,400
Roger.

245
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:39,320
Now, forward left leg.

246
00:12:39,320 --> 00:12:40,400
Keep her steady.

247
00:12:43,070 --> 00:12:47,070
It actually walks! I guess they did have
something to be proud of.

248
00:12:49,870 --> 00:12:51,580
What's wrong?

249
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:54,160
This is odd. The pressure inside
the reactor is increasing.

250
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:56,960
The temperature of the primary coolant
system is also rising!

251
00:12:56,960 --> 00:12:58,210
Open the release valve.

252
00:12:58,210 --> 00:12:59,630
Insert the neutron-deceleration fluid.

253
00:12:59,630 --> 00:13:00,550
No effect!

254
00:13:00,550 --> 00:13:02,210
The pump output isn't increasing!

255
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,550
Not good! Shut off the power.
Emergency stop!

256
00:13:07,550 --> 00:13:09,680
Abort signal transmission confirmed.

257
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:11,270
It's not accepting it!

258
00:13:11,270 --> 00:13:12,850
The radio circuit is being blocked!

259
00:13:12,850 --> 00:13:14,480
It's out of control!

260
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,640
It can't be!

261
00:13:18,270 --> 00:13:19,770
Run away!

262
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:32,910
That robot is as badly behaved
as the guy who built it.

263
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,130
The compression valve
is operating irregularly!

264
00:13:39,130 --> 00:13:40,880
The control rods aren't working!

265
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:43,510
At this rate, a meltdown is possible!

266
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,880
I don't believe it.

267
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:52,510
JA's been programmed to handle
all possible contingencies.

268
00:13:52,510 --> 00:13:54,680
This kind of thing can't happen!

269
00:13:54,680 --> 00:13:58,440
Yet, the fact is, the danger of
a meltdown is now before us!

270
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:02,940
Under the circumstances, our only option
is to wait for it to stop.

271
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:04,490
And what is the estimated probability
of an automatic stop?

272
00:14:04,490 --> 00:14:08,070
0.00002%! It would be a miracle!

273
00:14:08,070 --> 00:14:10,530
Determined efforts are better
than waiting for a miracle!

274
00:14:10,530 --> 00:14:12,530
Tell me how to stop that thing!

275
00:14:12,530 --> 00:14:14,120
We've tried every possible option.

276
00:14:14,120 --> 00:14:18,920
No, there's got to be a last resort,
a way to wipe everything out.

277
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,670
Give me the password.

278
00:14:20,670 --> 00:14:23,420
The password to delete all
programming is top secret.

279
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,920
I can't authorize it.

280
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,420
I'm not allowed to tell you!

281
00:14:26,420 --> 00:14:28,260
Then get the clearance!

282
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:28,930
Right now!

283
00:14:30,550 --> 00:14:33,310
It's me. Let me speak to
Mr. Manda in Tokyo-2.

284
00:14:33,310 --> 00:14:36,060
That's right, the Director of Internal Affairs.

285
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:39,900
Well, I've delegated this to Yasugi. Ask him.

286
00:14:41,690 --> 00:14:44,530
I can't give authorization for such
an important matter on the phone.

287
00:14:44,530 --> 00:14:47,070
Could you submit a formal written request?

288
00:14:47,070 --> 00:14:50,320
So, I just need to get
Mr. Yoshizawa's permission?

289
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:53,200
Yes, I've already got an approval
from Mr. Witz.

290
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,290
Yes... yes, okay.

291
00:14:55,290 --> 00:14:56,750
The evasion of responsibility...

292
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:58,710
A written order of clearance will be sent.

293
00:14:58,710 --> 00:15:00,250
That will make this an official operation.

294
00:15:00,250 --> 00:15:04,210
We can't wait for that! Once that thing
explodes, it'll be too late!

295
00:15:08,090 --> 00:15:11,510
Jet Alone is heading for Atsugi.

296
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:12,890
Time is running out.

297
00:15:12,890 --> 00:15:15,890
From here on, I'll be acting independently.

298
00:15:15,890 --> 00:15:17,350
Excuse me.

299
00:15:16,930 --> 00:15:18,430
Nerv Party

300
00:15:17,350 --> 00:15:18,890
Hey, Hyuga?

301
00:15:18,890 --> 00:15:23,440
I've arranged it with Atsugi, so bring Shinji
and Unit 01 equipped with the F module.

302
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:24,980
Yes, this is an emergency.

303
00:15:24,980 --> 00:15:27,360
This is pointless. Call this off,
Captain Katsuragi.

304
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:30,110
Besides, how do you plan to stop it?

305
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:32,200
By inputting a direct command manually.

306
00:15:34,950 --> 00:15:36,700
Are you serious?

307
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:37,660
Yes.

308
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:41,290
But the interior must be
flooded with radioactivity!

309
00:15:41,290 --> 00:15:42,290
It's too risky!

310
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:44,130
But if I make it, everyone will be saved.

311
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:50,420
The hatch can be opened manually
as soon as our control signal is cut off.

312
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:52,890
You'll be able to enter through the backpack.

313
00:15:54,010 --> 00:15:55,470
"Hope".

314
00:15:56,810 --> 00:15:59,020
That's the password to delete
the programming.

315
00:15:59,980 --> 00:16:00,930
Thank you.

316
00:16:06,110 --> 00:16:07,690
JA is the target.

317
00:16:07,690 --> 00:16:10,360
There's a danger of meltdown
within five minutes.

318
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:14,870
Therefore, we cannot allow it to get
any closer to a populated area.

319
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:15,490
Hyuga?

320
00:16:15,490 --> 00:16:16,200
Yes, Ma'am?

321
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:20,370
As soon as you drop off the Eva, break away
immediately and ascend to a safe altitude.

322
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:21,120
Roger.

323
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,370
And Shinji...

324
00:16:21,750 --> 00:16:22,370
Yes.

325
00:16:22,370 --> 00:16:25,580
Run alongside the target,
and place me on its back.

326
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:29,210
Then restrain the target as best you can.

327
00:16:29,210 --> 00:16:31,670
You're going inside?

328
00:16:31,670 --> 00:16:33,130
That's right.

329
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:33,800
That's crazy!

330
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:36,890
I know it's crazy, but there
just isn't any other way.

331
00:16:36,890 --> 00:16:38,720
But it's too dangerous!

332
00:16:38,720 --> 00:16:39,970
Don't worry.

333
00:16:39,970 --> 00:16:42,850
If it comes down to it, the Eva
can withstand a direct explosion.

334
00:16:42,850 --> 00:16:45,400
Not that! I meant for you, Miss Misato!

335
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:48,400
Well, I've got to give it my best shot,

336
00:16:48,400 --> 00:16:50,150
or else I'll regret it for the rest of my life.

337
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,610
Target sighted.

338
00:16:59,030 --> 00:17:00,330
Here we go.

339
00:17:04,960 --> 00:17:06,750
Eva in drop position.

340
00:17:06,750 --> 00:17:08,000
Docking release!

341
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:08,380
Roger!

342
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:28,520
We've caught up!

343
00:17:28,520 --> 00:17:31,110
We've got less than four minutes.
Put me on, now!

344
00:17:41,700 --> 00:17:43,330
That's fine! Just do it!

345
00:17:50,090 --> 00:17:52,170
Miss Misato!

346
00:17:55,880 --> 00:17:56,470
Be careful.

347
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,180
Talk about hot.

348
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:04,770
This looks bad.

349
00:18:04,770 --> 00:18:07,140
Stop, you bastard!

350
00:18:12,610 --> 00:18:14,030
Miss Misato! Hurry!

351
00:18:16,450 --> 00:18:17,070
This must be it.

352
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,000
HOPE

353
00:18:32,590 --> 00:18:33,840
Error?

354
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:35,130
What in the hell is this?

355
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:43,560
There's no doubt!
The program must have been altered!

356
00:18:50,350 --> 00:18:53,190
The power reactor is just
0.2 short of critical!

357
00:18:53,190 --> 00:18:55,280
The control rods won't function!

358
00:18:55,280 --> 00:18:57,360
Guess it's time to sink or swim.

359
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,920
Miss Misato, get out of there!

360
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:20,010
Move, damn you!

361
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:25,310
Miss Misato!

362
00:19:30,640 --> 00:19:32,770
0.1 to critical!

363
00:19:32,770 --> 00:19:34,610
It's no use! It's going to explode!

364
00:19:34,610 --> 00:19:35,940
It's all over.

365
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:36,860
Miss Misato!

366
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:01,470
She made it!

367
00:20:01,470 --> 00:20:02,430
Internal pressure decreasing!

368
00:20:02,430 --> 00:20:03,640
All readings are nominal!

369
00:20:03,640 --> 00:20:05,140
We're saved!

370
00:20:07,060 --> 00:20:09,640
We did it! We did it! We did it!

371
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:11,270
That idiot.

372
00:20:11,270 --> 00:20:13,190
Miss Misato, are you all right?!

373
00:20:13,190 --> 00:20:14,230
Miss Misato?!

374
00:20:14,230 --> 00:20:18,110
Yeah, but I feel like crap.

375
00:20:18,110 --> 00:20:22,610
I'm so glad you're alive! Thank goodness!

376
00:20:22,610 --> 00:20:24,240
Really, thank goodness!

377
00:20:24,240 --> 00:20:28,950
But that was really amazing! I'm so
impressed! It really was a miracle!

378
00:20:28,950 --> 00:20:30,250
Yeah...

379
00:20:30,250 --> 00:20:33,120
But the miracle was set up by someone.

380
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:37,670
Recovery of Unit 01 is complete.

381
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:39,920
No danger of radioactive contamination.

382
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,470
Except for Captain Katsuragi's actions,

383
00:20:41,470 --> 00:20:43,300
everything went according to plan.

384
00:20:43,300 --> 00:20:44,760
Good work.

385
00:20:55,060 --> 00:20:56,230
G'morning.

386
00:21:03,900 --> 00:21:06,870
Now for a morning shower!

387
00:21:06,870 --> 00:21:09,660
Where are my bra and panties?

388
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:15,750
Good morning, Ikari!

389
00:21:15,750 --> 00:21:17,170
Good morning.

390
00:21:17,170 --> 00:21:18,630
I'm taking off!

391
00:21:18,630 --> 00:21:20,050
See ya!

392
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:25,470
Miss Misato is just so cool!

393
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:27,590
I thought so too,

394
00:21:27,590 --> 00:21:32,930
but at home she's shameless.
She's so coarse, uncool, and really sloppy.

395
00:21:34,230 --> 00:21:36,480
It makes me embarrassed for her.

396
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:38,560
How nice for you.

397
00:21:40,270 --> 00:21:42,150
What do you mean?

398
00:21:42,150 --> 00:21:44,900
He really is a kid.

399
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:46,150
Yeah, he sure is.

400
00:21:46,150 --> 00:21:47,490
How's that?

401
00:21:47,490 --> 00:21:51,410
She lets you see a side of her that
she won't show to anyone else.

402
00:21:51,410 --> 00:21:53,450
That means she's your family.

403
00:21:57,790 --> 00:22:00,750
TO BE CONTINUED

404
00:23:06,230 --> 00:23:07,150
PREVIEW

405
00:23:07,900 --> 00:23:13,580
Eva Unit 02 and its pilot have left
Wilhelmshaven, Germany to come to Japan!

406
00:23:13,580 --> 00:23:18,120
The sudden attack of an Angel forces a first
submarine battle onto the activated Unit 02!

407
00:23:18,120 --> 00:23:20,460
It's the next episode: "Asuka Arrives in Japan"

408
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:21,210
ASUKA ARRIVES IN JAPAN
